"The patient underwent a robot-assisted radical prostatectomy with a pathological stage of pT3a, positive surgical margins, and no invasion of the seminal vesicles. The biopsy findings showed Gleason 3+3 in both peripheral zone and left base (mid) locations. No lymph nodes were removed, and nodal status is documented as pNx, which widens uncertainty as missing nodal sampling is relevant. The preoperative PSA was 2.4.\n\nPrognosis is influenced by the positive surgical margins and the T3a stage. The absence of lymphovascular invasion is a favorable finding. The biopsy grade was ISUP grade group 1, which contrasts with the surgical grade group 2. The prognosis is guided by a heuristic horizon suggesting a potential recurrence horizon around 46 months, with a sensitivity range spanning from 28 to 64 months. Postoperative PSA and its trajectory remain unknown due to missing previous notes. Information regarding postoperative PSA and its subsequent trajectory would revise this prognosis. The fixed estimated horizon is 45.96 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 27.58–64.35 months; its coverage has not been validated."
